eturn `1`; `bins = -3`/`-6` segfault). There is no \"expected\nC result\" to match, so the differential tests for rows 16–17 assert the only\nmeaningful invariant: **the Rust `.so` must not corrupt memory or crash**, and\nthey record the observed C behaviour. Rows 18–19 are not executed at all\n(a deliberate stack-exhaustion or a null dereference would abort the test\nprocess, not produce a comparable value).\n\nEvery other row (1–15) is fully defined C and is asserted bit-for-bit.\n\nThe well-defined domain of the API is therefore:\n* `spectral_contrast(a, b, length)` — any `length`; `a`/`b` must be readable for\n  `max(length,0)` `float`s.\n* `match(test, reference, bins, threshold)` — `bins >= 1`, `test`/`reference`\n  readable for `bins` `double`s, and `bins` small enough for two VLAs to fit on\n  the stack.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
